«
@@ ============================================================
@@ MolarMass — the molar mass of a chemical formula, as an interval
@@ Input : a formula as a text: "H2SO4", "Ca(OH)2", "CuSO4·5H2O"
@@ Output: M in g/mol, the sum of the standard atomic weights of its
@@         atoms (CIAAW 2024) times Mu = 1 g/mol (to 3.5E-10)
@@ The bounds of the intervals add up: M lies between the sums.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================
  ⓁFormula
  → flist
  «
    @ No accumulator before the first element: an unknown symbol leaves no 0
    flist 1 GET 1 GET ⓁAtWt flist 1 GET 2 GET *
    IF flist SIZE 1 > THEN
      2 flist SIZE FOR jx
        flist jx GET 1 GET ⓁAtWt flist jx GET 2 GET * +
      NEXT
    END
    1_(g/mol) *
  »
»
